    (5423, N'Draw Chart Text with Custom Font Sizes', N'CustomChartTextFonts.cs', N'C#', N'Indicator', N'draw text,chart text,custom font,font size,price label,Draw.Text,SimpleFont,TextAlignment', N'#region Using declarations
using System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations;
using System.Windows;
using System.Windows.Media;
using NinjaTrader.Gui.Tools;
using NinjaTrader.NinjaScript;
using NinjaTrader.NinjaScript.DrawingTools;
#endregion

namespace NinjaTrader.NinjaScript.Indicators
{
    public class SampleChangeFont : Indicator
    {
        private SimpleFont largeFont;
        private SimpleFont smallFont;

        protected override void OnStateChange()
        {
            if (State == State.SetDefaults)
            {
                Description = "Demonstrates how to draw chart text using different font sizes.";
                Name = "Sample Change Font";
                Calculate = Calculate.OnBarClose;
                IsOverlay = true;

                largeFont = new SimpleFont("Arial", 12);
                smallFont = new SimpleFont("Arial", 8);
            }
            else if (State == State.Terminated)
            {
                largeFont = null;
                smallFont = null;
            }
        }

        protected override void OnBarUpdate()
        {
            if (CurrentBar < 1)
                return;

            // Bullish bar: display the high using the larger font.
            if (Close[0] > Open[0])
            {
                Draw.Text(
                    this,
                    "highText",
                    true,
                    High[0].ToString(),
                    1,
                    High[0] + 2 * TickSize,
                    0,
                    Brushes.Green,
                    largeFont,
                    TextAlignment.Justify,
                    Brushes.Transparent,
                    Brushes.Transparent,
                    0);

                Draw.Text(
                    this,
                    "lowText",
                    true,
                    Low[0].ToString(),
                    1,
                    Low[0] - 2 * TickSize,
                    0,
                    Brushes.Red,
                    smallFont,
                    TextAlignment.Justify,
                    Brushes.Transparent,
                    Brushes.Transparent,
                    0);
            }
            // Bearish bar: display the low using the larger font.
            else if (Close[0] < Open[0])
            {
                Draw.Text(
                    this,
                    "highText",
                    true,
                    High[0].ToString(),
                    1,
                    High[0] + 2 * TickSize,
                    0,
                    Brushes.Green,
                    smallFont,
                    TextAlignment.Justify,
                    Brushes.Transparent,
                    Brushes.Transparent,
                    0);

                Draw.Text(
                    this,
                    "lowText",
                    true,
                    Low[0].ToString(),
                    1,
                    Low[0] - 2 * TickSize,
                    0,
                    Brushes.Red,
                    largeFont,
                    TextAlignment.Justify,
                    Brushes.Transparent,
                    Brushes.Transparent,
                    0);
            }
            // Neutral bar: display both prices using the smaller font.
            else
            {
                Draw.Text(
                    this,
                    "highText",
                    true,
                    High[0].ToString(),
                    1,
                    High[0] + 2 * TickSize,
                    0,
                    Brushes.Green,
                    smallFont,
                    TextAlignment.Justify,
                    Brushes.Transparent,
                    Brushes.Transparent,
                    0);

                Draw.Text(
                    this,
                    "lowText",
                    true,
                    Low[0].ToString(),
                    1,
                    Low[0] - 2 * TickSize,
                    0,
                    Brushes.Red,
                    smallFont,
                    TextAlignment.Justify,
                    Brushes.Transparent,
                    Brushes.Transparent,
                    0);
            }
        }

        #region Properties

        [NinjaScriptProperty]
        [Display(
            Name = "Large Font",
            Description = "Font used for emphasized chart text.",
            Order = 1,
            GroupName = "Font")]
        public SimpleFont LargeFont
        {
            get { return largeFont; }
            set { largeFont = value; }
        }

        [NinjaScriptProperty]
        [Display(
            Name = "Small Font",
            Description = "Font used for standard chart text.",
            Order = 2,
            GroupName = "Font")]
        public SimpleFont SmallFont
        {
            get { return smallFont; }
            set { smallFont = value; }
        }

        #endregion
